[end_timeline]
label Puck
green: Good morning.
worl: Hey Green. You know, We've been wondering.
cable: No one's ever seen you climb.
[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label group_b_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: I don't really need to? Doesn't really make my work more efficient
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: I can't.
else:
	green: No one's seen you climb either
[end_timeline]
label group_b
if {group_b} == true:
	kintan: group b final words
else:
	trim: test
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label group_a
if {group_a} == true:
	...
else:
	...so smug! You should've seen how Green shrugged me off.
	I need Haptor to stop comparing us, like I need to be reminded...
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label group_a_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: (You don't say anything)
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: Yeah he shouldn't have done that.
else:
	green: what are we talking about?
	That's literally none of your business
label Terminal
It's a little old and laggy, but we don't really have the parts to repair it. We do so much recycling though. If only we could have some of those pieces.
[end_timeline]
label Elevator
I don’t have the credentials to use it. Cable probably does.
[end_timeline]
label Locked Door
It’s rusting at the edges, which is weird because there’s no oxygen here anymore.
[end_timeline]